WEBVTT

00:01.130 --> 00:04.080
<b>During the Pre-Impossible Mission Planning</b>

00:03.330 --> 00:06.920
The time is 2 p.m., and Mr. Uwe is in the drawing room.

00:06.920 --> 00:09.670
The assassin's made their way into the manor
disguised as a deliveryman.

00:10.250 --> 00:12.080
They have a weapon concealed in their pocket.

00:12.330 --> 00:13.750
Let me think...

00:13.920 --> 00:17.580
I start by having Sara's animals
check them for firearms.

00:17.920 --> 00:21.380
They aren't carrying anything that
smells of gunpowder.

00:21.670 --> 00:22.920
The assassin advances.

00:23.290 --> 00:27.880
I station Lily and Sybilla on the
left and right to stand guard.

00:28.080 --> 00:31.540
The assassin turns the corner and
enters their blind spot.

00:32.080 --> 00:34.750
They kill a nearby maid.

00:34.750 --> 00:36.580
You lose your bead on their location.

00:43.170 --> 00:44.580
That wasn't bad.

00:44.580 --> 00:45.960
Let's go again.

00:45.960 --> 00:46.960
Are you up for it?

00:46.960 --> 00:48.460
Yes, of course.

00:48.460 --> 00:50.000
By the way, I have a question...

00:50.000 --> 00:52.210
The panties I'm wearing today are white.

00:52.210 --> 00:53.630
That wasn't what I was going to ask.
The panties I'm wearing today are white.<b></b>

00:53.880 --> 00:55.500
You really didn't have to finish that sentence.

00:55.500 --> 00:56.920
Just as I expected.

00:56.920 --> 01:00.330
I was actually hoping to ask about
something more serious.

01:00.630 --> 01:01.830
Serious how?

01:06.290 --> 01:10.080
Why weren't you able to take advantage of
your talents back at your academy?

01:11.080 --> 01:14.130
I have everyone's test scores and evaluations.

01:14.380 --> 01:17.380
Everyone else has logical reasons
for why they washed out.

01:17.920 --> 01:21.170
However, you're the one person
I don't have a good explanation for.

01:21.540 --> 01:22.750
What happened?

01:24.130 --> 01:27.290
I doubt you would believe me if I told you.

01:27.290 --> 01:30.380
I promise to accept whatever you tell me.

01:35.500 --> 01:37.130
I really appreciate that.

01:37.920 --> 01:39.540
The truth is,

01:39.830 --> 01:41.630
I'm not good with men.

01:47.460 --> 01:48.670
Boss?

01:48.920 --> 01:51.330
I'm sorry, I'm afraid I don't follow.

01:52.540 --> 01:57.500
Being around men makes my stomach start hurting.

01:57.500 --> 02:01.250
You seem fine around me, though.

02:01.250 --> 02:03.080
You're an exception, Boss.

02:03.460 --> 02:05.750
Well, that seems awfully convenient.

02:06.460 --> 02:07.670
That's fine, though.

02:07.670 --> 02:09.460
I did promise to accept your explanation.

02:10.250 --> 02:12.380
That love of yours is a mysterious thing.

02:12.380 --> 02:13.710
Is it?

02:14.460 --> 02:16.790
In that case, I have a question for you as well.

02:17.630 --> 02:20.460
Where did you get that cut on your hand?

02:21.920 --> 02:24.960
I had an urgent mission this afternoon,

02:24.960 --> 02:27.380
and embarrassingly, I got it caught on something.

02:27.710 --> 02:30.250
Your fatigue is starting to get you hurt.

02:30.580 --> 02:32.420
Please, you should go to bed.

02:32.630 --> 02:33.880
Don't worry about it.

02:34.210 --> 02:37.380
Besides, I have a backlog of reports
I need to get through.

02:40.670 --> 02:44.580
I'm not giving this fountain pen back
until you get some sleep.

02:46.540 --> 02:47.960
Magnificent.

02:48.250 --> 02:50.830
Very well, I'll turn in for the night.

02:50.830 --> 02:52.040
You can go ahead and-

02:52.040 --> 02:54.210
Of course, I'll get in bed with you
and sing you a lullaby.

02:54.710 --> 02:55.920
Get out.

02:58.580 --> 03:00.250
You must be tired too.

03:00.580 --> 03:03.880
I'll be asleep soon,
so please get the lights on your way-

03:05.710 --> 03:07.080
That was fast.

03:13.630 --> 03:16.830
Did you let your guard down because
it was me you were with?

03:22.960 --> 03:25.170
Have you come to want to let me dote on you,

03:25.170 --> 03:27.130
even just a little?

03:30.040 --> 03:34.420
I'm under no illusions about my love ever bearing fruit.

03:35.540 --> 03:37.000
But even so,

03:37.000 --> 03:41.080
once I complete the mission and make you proud,

03:41.880 --> 03:46.250
would it be greedy of me to hope for
just one percent of your affection?

04:06.920 --> 04:11.420
SPY CLASSROOM

04:12.750 --> 04:15.880
Itami ga unda daishou

04:15.880 --> 04:23.170
Nido to kienai kasabuta wo dakishime

04:23.170 --> 04:28.540
Gouin na sukimakaze ano hi sarawareta

04:28.540 --> 04:33.210
Kawarenai boku wa oiteikanakucha

04:33.500 --> 04:38.420
Nee fuan sae oikoshite

04:38.420 --> 04:41.790
Shiranakatta sora to kyou wa kono ashi de

04:41.790 --> 04:44.630
Chouyou wo mukaeyou

04:45.080 --> 04:47.670
Fukou ga kureta shiawase

04:47.670 --> 04:50.420
Zetsubou no hate ni mieta

04:50.420 --> 04:55.710
Shirube wa ima hitosuji no hi wo tomosu

04:55.710 --> 04:58.130
Karamiau kako wo harae

04:58.130 --> 05:06.040
Kokoro ga hokorobu basho made aragau

05:06.040 --> 05:11.920
Ah, shunkan ikinobiro

05:18.460 --> 05:25.290
<b>MISSION: Daughter Dearest III</b>

05:19.710 --> 05:20.830
Tomorrow evening,

05:20.830 --> 05:23.290
there's going to be a dinner party at the mansion.

05:23.290 --> 05:25.290
The attendees are just going to be politicians

05:25.290 --> 05:27.290
and other political bigwigs who share Mr. Uwe's views,

05:27.290 --> 05:29.670
but we need to be prepared for anything
that might happen.

05:30.040 --> 05:33.290
Sara, I need you to keep watch over
the mansion starting tonight.

05:33.290 --> 05:34.670
Will do.

05:34.670 --> 05:37.380
Now, what can you tell me about
the incident the other night?

05:37.380 --> 05:41.630
Sadly, there weren't any clues in the traps we set.

05:42.630 --> 05:45.130
This little guy couldn't even pick up the bad guy's scent,

05:45.130 --> 05:47.080
so they must have come prepared.

05:47.500 --> 05:48.500
I see.

05:48.500 --> 05:50.210
B-by the way,

05:50.210 --> 05:53.540
do you think there's a chance the assassin
will come back tomorrow?

05:53.960 --> 05:56.460
It's a possibility,
which is why we're staying on high alert.

05:56.460 --> 05:58.500
R-right...

05:59.960 --> 06:02.210
Don't worry, I'll be fine.

06:02.210 --> 06:03.880
I'm ready to give it my all!

06:04.790 --> 06:06.080
That's reassuring to hear.

06:07.460 --> 06:09.130
I have instructions from the boss:

06:09.330 --> 06:13.540
"Chisel Mr. Uwe like you were chiseling
a rock from the bottom of the sea."

06:13.540 --> 06:15.960
What's that in normal-person talk?

06:16.170 --> 06:19.170
I believe he wants you to get Uwe to tell you details

06:19.170 --> 06:21.540
about the people who'll be
attending the function tomorrow.

06:21.540 --> 06:22.830
On it.

06:25.920 --> 06:27.500
What's good, Uwe?

06:27.500 --> 06:29.920
We should start thinkin' about heading out, yeah?

06:29.920 --> 06:32.210
It's an hour earlier than usual.

06:32.210 --> 06:34.460
Yeah, but the weather's not gonna hold.

06:34.710 --> 06:36.420
Besides, if we get there early,

06:36.420 --> 06:38.880
you can tell me all about the people
who'll be comin' tomorrow.

06:39.750 --> 06:43.420
I'm going to go plant more bugs around
the mansion to get ready for the party.

06:44.040 --> 06:48.210
Lily, would you mind distracting the
other residents for me while I do?

06:48.210 --> 06:49.750
Leave it to me!

06:49.750 --> 06:55.290
I figured you'd ask, so I actually already knocked over
a bucket and soaked the hallway downstairs.

06:55.710 --> 06:58.880
I think I might've developed a knack for precognition-

06:59.420 --> 07:02.630
Shoot! I didn't think she'd find it 'til later!
Who did this?! Who poured water everywhere?!<b></b>

07:03.170 --> 07:06.790
<i>Lily's bold moves make for a perfect diversion.</i>

07:07.330 --> 07:08.830
<i>Everything's going smoothly.</i>

07:09.080 --> 07:11.880
<b>The Next Day</b>

07:49.420 --> 07:51.130
<i>No intruders.</i>

07:51.500 --> 07:54.250
<i>I went through the pockets of
everyone who seemed sketchy,</i>

07:54.250 --> 07:55.830
<i>but none of 'em had any weapons.</i>

07:56.290 --> 07:58.500
<i>Sara didn't see anything out of the ordinary, either.</i>

07:58.500 --> 08:01.290
<i>And Lily even got through her maid work
without screwing up for a change.</i>

08:01.290 --> 08:03.960
Probably 'cuz your instructions were so dang good.

08:03.960 --> 08:05.000
Oh, not at all.

08:05.000 --> 08:07.500
If anything, I should be the one complimenting you all.

08:07.500 --> 08:09.540
I spent the entire party hiding away in the back.

08:10.000 --> 08:11.630
By the way, Grete,

08:11.630 --> 08:15.830
you said you came from a politician's family, right?

08:16.500 --> 08:18.040
I did. What about it?

08:18.500 --> 08:21.080
Did you spend a bunch of time at
high society shindigs like this one?

08:21.080 --> 08:22.920
I'm kinda jealous.

08:22.920 --> 08:25.040
It's like, it's all so swanky.

08:26.040 --> 08:27.250
Not quite.

08:28.130 --> 08:30.960
I never could find a place for myself in this world.

08:33.040 --> 08:34.040
That so?

08:36.080 --> 08:37.290
Grete!

08:38.330 --> 08:39.580
Could I speak with you?

08:47.000 --> 08:50.000
Why'd you spend the whole party over in the kitchen?

08:50.460 --> 08:53.880
I wanted you out on the floor mingling with the guests.

08:53.880 --> 08:55.460
My deepest apologies.

08:55.460 --> 08:57.000
I wasn't feeling well,

08:57.000 --> 08:59.380
but I figured I could at least help by
washing dishes and cleaning up.

08:59.500 --> 09:02.210
The world of politics is dominated by men, you know.

09:02.210 --> 09:04.880
Having a couple of cute young maids going
around with smiles on their faces

09:04.880 --> 09:07.170
helps make parties like ours run that much smoother.

09:08.040 --> 09:09.040
I see.

09:09.040 --> 09:10.670
So, what's the deal?

09:11.420 --> 09:12.630
Did you just feel like slacking off?

09:12.630 --> 09:14.580
<i>If I tell her that I have problems dealing with men,</i>

09:14.580 --> 09:18.210
<i>she'll see me as unfit to be a maid,
and she might even fire me.</i>

09:18.670 --> 09:21.710
<i>That said, the more lies I pile on, the more likely
my whole story is to eventually fall apart.</i>

09:21.710 --> 09:22.960
Grete?

09:23.380 --> 09:26.880
T-to tell you the truth,
there's someone I'm quite in love with,

09:26.880 --> 09:28.290
so getting close to other men doesn't-

09:29.080 --> 09:30.630
That changes everything!

09:30.630 --> 09:31.830
Spill, girl!

09:32.170 --> 09:33.710
I-if you insist.

09:34.290 --> 09:36.960
It's what you would call lovesickness.

09:36.960 --> 09:40.880
When I think of him, it makes me
not want to talk to other men.

09:40.880 --> 09:43.130
Oh, was it that guy from the other day?

09:43.130 --> 09:46.880
I saw Sybilla and Lily talking to a total hunk
right after the assassin attacked.

09:46.880 --> 09:49.080
Skinny guy, long hair!

09:49.710 --> 09:51.500
No, someone else.

09:51.500 --> 09:53.540
That man's just a teacher from our school.

09:53.540 --> 09:56.540
I suspect he was just dropping by
his students' job site to check in on us.

09:56.540 --> 09:59.500
He's not the guy, huh?

09:59.960 --> 10:01.460
Can I have him, then?

10:01.460 --> 10:02.460
Huh?

10:02.460 --> 10:04.210
I mean, a schoolteacher like him?

10:04.210 --> 10:06.000
He's probably all kinds of pent up.

10:06.000 --> 10:09.210
All I'd have to do is get some drinks in him and pretend
to be tipsy so I could press my chest against him,

10:09.210 --> 10:11.580
and I could get him into bed and
let nature take its course.

10:13.710 --> 10:15.130
Would you look at that?

10:15.130 --> 10:16.880
You can make faces like that after all.

10:19.580 --> 10:21.460
I'm kidding, I'm kidding.

10:21.460 --> 10:23.420
Look, I've got nothing against lovesickness,

10:23.420 --> 10:25.540
just make sure it doesn't get in the way of your job.

10:25.540 --> 10:28.880
Besides, men flock to good-looking gals like us.

10:28.880 --> 10:30.830
You don't have to take life so seriously.

10:31.710 --> 10:34.420
Needy women don't get loved.

10:35.580 --> 10:37.710
I despise that philosophy.

10:38.250 --> 10:40.880
I can't stand people who don't put in the work

10:40.880 --> 10:42.710
to be worthy of love.

10:43.750 --> 10:44.960
Excuse me?

10:49.420 --> 10:52.250
Isn't that right there the reason nobody loves you?

10:52.250 --> 10:54.380
Oh, I hit the nail on the head.

10:58.750 --> 11:00.170
We're done here.

11:00.170 --> 11:02.290
The room feels darker just having you in it.

11:02.290 --> 11:04.540
If you look like you're fighting back
a grimace the whole time,

11:04.540 --> 11:06.710
you'll just bring down the mood
at the parties anyways.

11:07.790 --> 11:09.080
By your leave, then.

11:14.790 --> 11:17.130
<i>That was made in Galgad.</i>

11:17.710 --> 11:20.080
That's a very pretty brooch.

11:20.080 --> 11:22.170
It was a present from my boyfriend.

11:22.460 --> 11:23.670
What about it?

11:23.670 --> 11:25.130
Nothing, I was just saying.

11:36.290 --> 11:38.580
<i>I'm so tired.</i>

11:39.000 --> 11:41.540
Isn't that right there the reason nobody loves you?

11:41.830 --> 11:44.040
<i>I know that.
How could I not?</i>

11:50.080 --> 11:52.250
I never got a chance to give it back.

11:53.000 --> 11:54.000
Boss...

11:58.880 --> 11:59.880
Hello?

12:00.290 --> 12:01.830
Long day, huh?

12:01.830 --> 12:03.710
Lily? Did something-

12:03.710 --> 12:05.880
Nah, you just stay right where you are.

12:08.170 --> 12:09.420
Pat, pat...

12:09.420 --> 12:10.540
Um...

12:10.540 --> 12:14.710
You looked super tired,
so I thought I'd pamper you a bit.

12:14.830 --> 12:18.000
Sorry it's my hands and not Teach's.

12:18.710 --> 12:21.080
Dang, you've got all kinds of knots.

12:21.080 --> 12:22.670
It makes sense, though,

12:22.670 --> 12:25.170
considering the unreal amount of work you're doing.

12:25.170 --> 12:26.830
You're giving me too much credit.

12:27.290 --> 12:29.380
And she's humble, to boot!

12:29.960 --> 12:32.830
You have a very impressive figure, Lily.

12:33.420 --> 12:34.830
Where's this coming from?!

12:34.830 --> 12:37.420
I've tried to seduce the boss so many times,

12:37.420 --> 12:39.710
but the constant failures are
starting to make me nervous.

12:39.710 --> 12:42.580
Nah, c'mon, don't beat yourself up about it.

12:42.580 --> 12:44.670
I mean, your figure is plenty...

12:45.210 --> 12:46.210
Uh...

12:46.460 --> 12:47.670
Plenty what?

12:48.330 --> 12:50.580
Plenty good for crossdressing with.

12:52.000 --> 12:54.500
Th-that's our resident master of disguise for you.

12:54.500 --> 12:57.460
She's such an expert, she doesn't even need
a chest binder to pass as a man!

12:57.460 --> 13:00.830
Why, it's basically like she's
crossdressing twenty-four-seven!

13:02.380 --> 13:04.630
Would it be all right if I broke your pinky finger?

13:04.630 --> 13:06.000
You're that pissed?!

13:07.170 --> 13:08.670
Don't you worry.

13:08.670 --> 13:12.080
There're loads of charming things about you.

13:12.630 --> 13:15.790
That's why no matter what happens,
we'll always be friends.

13:23.290 --> 13:27.000
I find it hard to imagine there being
anything charming about me at all.

13:27.330 --> 13:30.290
Who would ever love a girl like you?!

13:31.080 --> 13:33.710
Why can't you even smile like a normal person?!

13:35.040 --> 13:38.920
Why was I burdened with a daughter
as creepy as you?!

13:49.630 --> 13:51.330
Androphobia, huh?

13:51.880 --> 13:56.170
Her father all but forced her to enroll in her academy.

13:56.460 --> 14:00.290
The official story is that she's living overseas
as part of the treatment for some illness.

14:01.460 --> 14:05.920
In other words, her politician father
basically abandoned her.

14:06.630 --> 14:10.750
It says here she chose the code name
Daughter Dearest herself,

14:12.130 --> 14:16.460
but I'm sure there are plenty of things these
scraps of paper can't possibly tell me about her.

14:21.710 --> 14:23.420
Now, it's high time we started...

14:24.920 --> 14:26.580
this assassin hunt of ours.

14:28.250 --> 14:31.790
<b>MISSION: Daughter Dearest III</b>

14:35.960 --> 14:39.290
This is a list of the politicians we suspect
were killed by Corpse.

14:39.630 --> 14:42.290
Corpse's primary MO is making it look like
the victims committed suicide

14:42.290 --> 14:43.670
by jumping to their deaths.

14:43.670 --> 14:46.330
It doesn't use weapons, so it's hard to trace.

14:46.330 --> 14:48.130
There are probably all loads
of other assassinations

14:48.130 --> 14:51.170
that have been written off as suicides
that we just don't know about.

14:51.210 --> 14:52.790
That's so messed up.

14:52.790 --> 14:55.790
Many of the dead politicians were people
who devoted everything they had

14:55.790 --> 14:58.040
to getting our nation back on its feet after the war.

14:58.040 --> 14:59.290
Losing them hurts.

14:59.380 --> 15:01.830
<i>So, this is why they call it a shadow war.</i>

15:02.380 --> 15:03.380
Sara...

15:03.960 --> 15:05.380
Don't worry.

15:05.380 --> 15:08.330
As the World's Strongest,
I'll make sure I put Corpse down.

15:08.830 --> 15:10.250
There's no need to be so afraid.

15:13.750 --> 15:15.330
I-I have to tell you!

15:15.790 --> 15:18.130
I know it's pathetic,
but hearing that made me feel better.

15:18.420 --> 15:21.210
I'm glad you've started relying on us,

15:21.210 --> 15:25.630
but if I'm being totally honest, I feel a lot safer
when I know you're protecting us.

15:26.630 --> 15:28.080
That's nothing to be ashamed of.

15:28.080 --> 15:32.210
But, um, that's why I think you should
pay more attention to Miss Grete.

15:32.670 --> 15:38.500
I don't know if you realize just how much courage
it takes her to do what she's doing.

15:40.080 --> 15:41.290
Duly noted.

15:49.210 --> 15:50.420
Uwe!

15:50.420 --> 15:51.830
Damn you, killer!

15:51.830 --> 15:53.540
What the hell do you think you're doin', dumbass?!

15:55.960 --> 15:58.420
You should know that
givin' your opponent a clear shot

15:58.420 --> 16:00.330
is about the most dangerous thing you can do.

16:00.330 --> 16:01.880
R-right.

16:03.710 --> 16:04.710
You hurt?

16:04.710 --> 16:06.170
Not a scratch.

16:06.170 --> 16:08.130
And it's all thanks to you, White.

16:08.540 --> 16:13.080
When you moved my bed away from the window,
it made it into a blind spot.

16:13.080 --> 16:15.250
I was able to escape his shots unscathed.

16:15.580 --> 16:18.670
Dang, that was a lucky-ass coincidence.

16:18.670 --> 16:20.040
I saw him.

16:20.040 --> 16:22.130
It was that man with the hideous birthmark.

16:22.130 --> 16:23.460
You actually got a good look at him?

16:23.460 --> 16:26.920
My eyes have gotten a lot better
since you lot started cooking for me.

16:26.920 --> 16:30.130
The next time he shows it will be
the day he meets his maker.

16:30.130 --> 16:33.000
Look, you wanna think about hiring a security guard?

16:33.330 --> 16:35.290
This guy's shown up twice in a single week.

16:35.830 --> 16:37.420
No price is too high

16:37.420 --> 16:39.210
when it comes to keepin' your family safe.

16:40.960 --> 16:42.710
I wouldn't do that if I were you.

16:46.000 --> 16:49.040
Welcoming more outsiders into the house
can't possibly be a good idea,

16:49.040 --> 16:52.080
not when you have no idea who the assassin might be.

16:52.080 --> 16:53.750
I'm terrified at the very thought.

16:53.750 --> 16:55.420
B-but...

16:55.420 --> 16:59.880
If anything, shouldn't you think about firing
the intruders who only just got here?

17:00.580 --> 17:02.040
What the hell are you on about?

17:02.040 --> 17:03.790
Who do you think it was that saved Uwe just-

17:03.790 --> 17:06.830
You know, you don't seem frightened by any of this.

17:06.830 --> 17:08.290
Neither do the other two.

17:08.290 --> 17:10.830
You were so brave during the first attack.

17:10.830 --> 17:13.290
Are you used to things like this?
Why is that?

17:13.540 --> 17:15.960
Was you moving the bed really just a coincidence?

17:16.880 --> 17:21.330
Uwe, don't you think we should look into
the girls' backgrounds again?

17:21.790 --> 17:25.920
For example, we could start with a thorough
inspection of their personal effects.

17:25.920 --> 17:27.290
You can't...

17:27.290 --> 17:29.040
Just so you know, Olivia...

17:32.210 --> 17:35.040
it's dangerous to pick up glass with your bare hands.

17:36.040 --> 17:37.250
<i>Glass?</i>

17:41.750 --> 17:43.000
You're so right!

17:43.000 --> 17:44.960
I cut my finger a little.

17:47.420 --> 17:48.710
I need to go wash up.

17:56.670 --> 17:59.710
When did Olivia grab that glass shard?

18:00.290 --> 18:02.080
If she had wanted to, she could've-

18:02.080 --> 18:05.040
Sybilla, please focus on your maid work for now.

18:06.670 --> 18:09.920
Say, what's that punk Klaus got to say about all this?

18:11.040 --> 18:13.130
He says to leave everything to me.

18:14.210 --> 18:16.330
He really trusts you that much?

18:16.580 --> 18:19.710
Also, where is he even?

18:23.710 --> 18:28.210
Sybilla, I'll handle the cleanup in here.

18:28.330 --> 18:30.750
Would you mind taking Uwe to another room?

18:30.750 --> 18:32.540
Y-you got it.

18:41.250 --> 18:43.670
<i>I have the situation under control.</i>

18:44.290 --> 18:46.460
<i>The enemy is starting to show their true colors.</i>

18:46.920 --> 18:49.880
<i>I need to start making preparations for the showdown.</i>

18:50.380 --> 18:52.670
<i>From here on out,
I can't afford to make a single mistake.</i>

18:52.880 --> 18:54.380
<i>If I screw up...</i>

18:58.630 --> 19:02.750
<i>I'll revise the plan as many times as it takes.</i>

19:03.500 --> 19:05.880
<i>I just need a little more time...</i>

19:10.210 --> 19:12.460
Are you okay, Grete?

19:13.420 --> 19:14.790
I-I'm terribly sorry.

19:14.790 --> 19:18.040
My foot slipped a little, but I'm fine now.

19:18.040 --> 19:19.250
No, you're not.

19:20.040 --> 19:21.880
You need another massage.

19:21.880 --> 19:25.880
I'm gonna knead you up until your whole
body's as mushy as a jellyfish.

19:26.670 --> 19:28.080
Y-you really don't...

19:30.580 --> 19:31.790
M-may I ask...

19:32.040 --> 19:33.630
Tricked you.

19:34.540 --> 19:37.170
Secure the target!

19:38.960 --> 19:41.000
Wh-what exactly are you doing?

19:41.000 --> 19:43.500
Enemies are to be brutally interrogated.

19:43.500 --> 19:44.960
Wh-what do you plan on doing with that?

19:44.960 --> 19:47.330
Here, we show our enemies no mercy.

19:48.420 --> 19:50.630
B-but yesterday, you said we would always be friends.

19:50.630 --> 19:51.630
I was fibbing.

19:51.630 --> 19:54.210
Don't you think there are some lies
you really shouldn't tell?

19:54.880 --> 19:58.130
If you thought we were gonna be the ones
getting conned forever...

19:58.790 --> 20:00.420
then you were dead wrong.

20:02.330 --> 20:03.580
A listening device?

20:03.580 --> 20:04.790
When did you...

20:04.790 --> 20:06.330
So, the guy with the birthmark...

20:07.080 --> 20:10.250
That was secretly you in disguise, wasn't it?

20:16.130 --> 20:17.830
I surrender.

20:18.000 --> 20:20.750
You're right, it was me all alon-

20:20.750 --> 20:23.080
This is so much fun!

20:23.460 --> 20:25.500
So, why'd you do it?

20:25.500 --> 20:28.960
I-I was about to tell you, but then you distracted me!

20:28.960 --> 20:31.630
Your reactions are so cute, I couldn't help myself.

20:36.790 --> 20:41.630
I disguised myself as the assassin
so could watch how any maids and guards reacted.

20:42.130 --> 20:45.580
That way, I could see if any of them
had undergone special training.

20:45.880 --> 20:48.250
Don't you think it's time you looped us in?

20:48.710 --> 20:50.630
What's this mission really about?

20:50.960 --> 20:52.170
But...

20:52.330 --> 20:54.420
You're incredible, Grete.

20:54.960 --> 21:00.420
In the end, none of the rest of us were able to tell
the boss that we wanted to share his burden.

21:01.130 --> 21:02.960
But now, I'll say this:

21:02.960 --> 21:06.710
I want to share your burden, Grete.

21:09.170 --> 21:10.420
Ditto to that.

21:10.420 --> 21:11.670
Me too.

21:14.330 --> 21:15.710
All right...

21:17.000 --> 21:19.040
Please listen, everyone.

21:19.330 --> 21:20.830
Our target, Corpse, is actually-

21:20.830 --> 21:24.000
I figured you kids were operatives.

21:24.830 --> 21:28.460
Well, fine, we can ditch the subtlety this time.

21:30.040 --> 21:31.460
Get to the window!

21:40.210 --> 21:41.630
Round two!

21:45.380 --> 21:46.580
Mr. Bernard!

21:51.250 --> 21:52.830
MR. BERNARD!

21:56.000 --> 21:57.500
Where's Teach?!

21:57.500 --> 21:59.000
We need to get him here, fast!

21:59.460 --> 22:00.670
He's not here.

22:01.500 --> 22:04.460
The boss won't be coming for us.

22:05.330 --> 22:09.830
This is a battle we have to win on our own.

22:11.330 --> 22:14.790
Furishikiru yoru o zutto nagameteta

22:14.790 --> 22:17.460
Doredake chikazuitemo

22:17.460 --> 22:19.710
(Give it up, give it up)

22:20.040 --> 22:23.670
Himitsu no namae sotto watasetara

22:23.670 --> 22:29.330
Mitsukaranai you ni kurayami ni toketeiku

22:36.920 --> 22:40.580
Kossori naiteta koto mo wasurechatta

22:40.580 --> 22:44.080
Saibou ga irekawatta mitai

22:44.080 --> 22:46.460
Betsu no hito ni nattari

22:46.790 --> 22:50.170
Isogashii hibi motto fuzakeyou ne

22:50.170 --> 22:52.960
Chotto kimi to hanashitai kedo

22:52.960 --> 22:55.210
Daremo mou inai

22:55.210 --> 22:58.960
Yakusokuda nante

22:58.960 --> 23:02.420
Sonna mono janai deshou

23:04.460 --> 23:08.000
Furishikiru yoru o zutto nagameteta

23:08.000 --> 23:10.830
Doredake chikazuitemo

23:10.830 --> 23:13.080
(Give it up, give it up)

23:13.380 --> 23:17.040
Himitsu no namae sotto watasetara

23:17.040 --> 23:22.210
Mitsukaranai you ni kurayami ni toketeiku

23:22.210 --> 23:23.670
Soshite umarekawatte

23:23.670 --> 23:26.000
Massara na yozora wo tobimawatte

23:26.000 --> 23:30.580
Nando mo kousa kimi to watashi

23:30.750 --> 23:32.250
Suihei na hoshi ni tatte

23:32.250 --> 23:34.790
Masugu na hitomi de mitsumeatte

23:34.790 --> 23:39.500
Mata aeta toki ni watashitai yo
